# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# transient build/commit artifacts (never the source of truth)
*.staging
*.staging-*
citygov.db.bak
# dossier PDFs of a local `./build.sh --pdf` (not published; a plain build
# drops the PDF column from dossiers/index.html again)
dossiers/*.pdf
# classify.py's review proposals (inventory/<dir>.classified.json)
inventory/*.classified.json

# run outputs (citation_todo.txt, quality_review.txt, raw logs): every writer
# creates the directory, so a fresh clone builds without it
logs/

# OS
.DS_Store

# an old local copy of the canton's source forms; no script uses it any more
# (ingest_new.py copies new files straight into the tracked formulare/)
forms/

# NOTE: citygov.db (the source of truth) and the generated artefacts
# (data_export.json, verlauf.json, dashboard.html, flows.html, index.html,
# 404.html, citygov_*.json[l], dossiers/, datentresor.db) ARE committed, so the
# worked example opens straight from the repo. The generated ones are only ever
# regenerated by ./build.sh, never hand-edited: dashboard.html, flows.html,
# index.html, 404.html, dossiers/*.html and dossiers/_repo.js carry a GENERATED
# banner, citygov_llm.json, citygov_ech_schemas.json, citygov_prefill.json and
# citygov_verzeichnis.json a meta block, datentresor.db a meta row,
# data_export.json a generated_at stamp, verlauf.json a «hinweis» naming its
# writer (export_json.py adds one entry per build day; past days can only be
# rebuilt with scripts/backfill_verlauf.py); the two .jsonl files carry no
# marker (writer: export_llm.py); schema/*.schema.json and exportvertrag.json
# (the export contract) say in their text that the exporters write them through
# scripts/export_vertrag.py.

# local DB safety snapshots (never committed)
citygov.db.backup-*

# key of the synthetic Datentresor (never committed; see README)
datentresor.key

# Python virtualenv
.venv/

# editor / tooling residue
.Rapp.history
*.Rhistory
# lock files Office and LibreOffice leave next to an opened file
~$*
.~lock.*#
